{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine","id":482979,"title":"Prometheans and the God Machine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-16T17:53:41-07:00","id":482979,"title":"Prometheans and the God Machine","content":"This is likely a well-trod subject, and no doubt many would prefer to keep these cosmologies separate, but for those interested in the intersection of the two I had a thought to bounce off the board.<br /> <br /> What if Prometheans are basically &quot;bugs&quot; in the God Machine? An unintended side-effect of a core function (The Principle) that the GM can no longer control. Disquiet and Wasteland are the result of Azoth causing the local GM programming to glitch out and corrupt. In this concept I would also posit that the GM is actively opposed (in as much as it is &quot;actively&quot; anything) to the Promethean Pilgrimage. When a Promethean achieves the New Dawn those bugs become fully integrated into the system and could threaten to compromise the entire design.<br /> <br /> Again, not an underlying &quot;truth&quot; of the World of Darkness, just a crossover idea I personally find interesting. Discuss!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 04-16-2015, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T18:02:59-07:00","id":483003,"title":"","content":"My favorite explanation that I heard was that the GM and the Principle were formerly a singular Demiurge, but some horrible accident (or series of accident), possibly including the Fall of Atlantis and the Death of Father Wolf, cause them to split into the emotive, unpredictable Principle, born of untamed Pyros; and the God-Machine, a methodical, soul-less machine built of Arcane Physics. The two are unaware that anything's missing, resulting in neither bothering to seek each other out.<br /> <br /> In my personal cosmology, the Principle is the Empyrean, the Capital-T Truth, the Alpha and Omega, not only the ultimate God, but reality incarnate, and the God-Machine is a foreign invader. Maybe it's Autochthon, surviving the end of the Exalted universe, maybe he's the Top Dog Exarch, etc. Whatever it is, they're fighting it out. Prometheans are designed by the Principle as agents of Chaos, intended to disrupt society and as a result, break down the GM's Infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T18:22:05-07:00","id":483006,"title":"","content":"Officially, the God-Machine and the Principle are distinct things, and I prefer them that way<sup>*</sup>: in essence, the God-Machine is a rough analog of the gnostic concept of the Demiurge, while the Principle is a rough analog of the Creator. I've toyed with the notion of making the God-Machine be the Prodigal Demiurge described in <b>Magnum Opus</b>. <br /> <br /> <hr />* though I don't object to the God-Machine having its own version of the Created: I personally prefer the Unfleshed as cousins to the Prometheans with distinct Lineages, rather than as a sixth Lineage; and it wouldn't be too much of a leap to recast them as creations of the God-Machine rather than creations of the Principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T19:19:52-07:00","id":483082,"title":"","content":"In my personal games, I've always house-ruled that the God-Machine doesn't like Prometheans because Disquiet disrupts the ability for Infrastructure to function properly, especially Infrastructure dependent on people acting as expected. Like many others, I've cast the God-Machine in the role of Demiurge and the Principle in the role of Creator. I've always been tantalized by a quick blurb in the Demon: The Descent corebook that implies it's a valid strategy for Demons to lure <i>qashmallim </i>and angels into crossing paths because they usually operate at cross purposes and will often find themselves at an impasse other than to fight it out. At which point the Unchained should be very far away. The idea of the Unfleshed being a God-Machine attempt to design Prometheans is always a fun one as well.<br /> <br /> In my personal cosmology, the God-Machine is a imperfect copy of the Principle from the future, designed by humans as a way to maintain homeostasis and the status quo because they managed to discover, measure, and understand the plans of the Principle and they were afraid of how it would change humanity in its relentless cycles of creation and evolution. It was sent back in time to make sure this wouldn't happen, and was preparing to oppose the Principle long before the Principle even 'thought' about using manifestations of its power to manipulate its interest. (IE. <i>qashmallim </i>and <i>lilithim</i>) It's been fighting a losing battle ever since then. Because of the time restrictions and &quot;one shot&quot; nature of <i>qashmallim</i> missions, I've painted the Principle as more respecting of free will. It's totally okay with its agents doing horrible things, using hallucinations to dellude you, etc. but it won't force someone to do something against their will. The God-Machine is... less forgiving, and it's agents don't run on a limited clock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T19:29:03-07:00","id":483085,"title":"","content":"The OP's idea raises a few questions. First, why are the angels best known to the Created <i>qashmallim</i> instead of the machine angels? Seems they would be intent on eliminating the Prometheans, and it would take an angel in most cases to have a chance. Also, what is it about the Redeemed that makes them dangerous to the design? Once transmuted, the Redeemed are functionally little different from the rest of humanity. The Redeemed are immaculate; does their lack of an ancestry throw errors into the G-M's calculations, or does the dross of their extinguished Azoth corrode the gears? If the Pyros is a core function of the Machine, what is that function, and how does it serve the Machine's larger function, and why are the <i>qashmallim</i> so dependent on the Prometheans for aid in their Missions? Why does the Pyros seem so essentially different from the God-Machine?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T15:48:03-07:00","id":486779,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">I like the take on it, it plays up nicely with the theme of God-Machine as the prime mover of the status quo. I think it could go a little further if the Supernal is added into the mix. Consider this: </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u200bThe supernal holds the source of all existence in the material world. A supreme being is theorized to exist, known by some scholars as the Corpus Mysteriorum, the body of magic. However, whether they are ancient humans ascended or the symbol of human ambition and domination, the Exarchs have shifted the material world into a black iron prison of souls. The God-Machine is an emanation of the Exarchs control, it maintains the status quo of reality. This is why the Machine's angels use essence, one of the most abundant sources of supernatural fuel in the world. The Principle is an emanation of something different. Perhaps it's derived from the Oracles (where watchtowers are keyed to elements, so are promethean humors) as a function to restore souls trapped in the abyss. Perhaps it's an emanation of the supernal human quality for introspection. Maybe it too is part of the Exarchs cast down as their doubts and sorrows for what has become of humanity and the world. Regardless of the reason, this emanation burns the black iron prison with fires of change and entropy, creating wastelands and disquiet.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">I think that might be fairly crossover friendly, as you can have mages, demons, and Prometheans all working towards the same philosophical ends.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4725-murder_of_craws","name":"Murder_of_Craws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4725_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T15:49:00-07:00","id":486782,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">I also really like Matt McFarland's musings on the two cosmic entities:</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>In The World of Darkness According to Matt: </b><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Principle was first. The Principle is many things \u2013 the spark of humanity, the desire for human connection, the lightning that created life from the primordial soup. Throughout the first few billion years of Earth, it was evolving along with all of life, looking for\u2026something. It was undergoing its own Pilgrimage.</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Once humanity arose, it found its purpose. It was able to shape servants \u2013 the <i>qashmallim</i> \u2013 from its endless reserve of Divine Fire, and send them into the world. Unfortunately, its own commitment to self-determination meant that it can\u2019t really control <i>qashmallim</i>; they always have a bit of autonomy (which is why they fail sometimes).</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Somewhere along the way, someone created the first Promethean. Might have been <a href=\"http://ptc-playtest.livejournal.com/17588.html\" target=\"_blank\">Hank</a>, actually, or it might have been some collection of rocks arranged into a human form that some caveman, lonely after the destruction of his tribe, created. Who knows. But at that point, the Principle\u2019s real purpose was cemented \u2013 guide the Pilgrimage of the Created. That is its chosen expression of its purpose.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">And then there\u2019s the God-Machine. The God-Machine is from the future, but the thing about time travel is that it\u2019s irrelevant <i>when </i>it happens, as long as it does. The God-Machine has its own agenda, but its agenda is a lot more complicated than the Principle\u2019s. In order to interact with the world, though, the God-Machine copied a lot of the Principle\u2019s \u201csoftware.\u201d That\u2019s why its angels always have enough free will to Fall.</span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4725-murder_of_craws","name":"Murder_of_Craws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4725_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T16:46:58-07:00","id":486832,"title":"","content":"I'm fond of the general notion that that Principle has more resonance with the Shadow and the Machine has more resonance with the Underworld; their respective descriptions seem to explain their respective sympathies in this fashion:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Scintillating Flame - Qashmallim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pyros permeates the entire physical world in small quantities, <b>wherever humans (and other beings) plan, act on impulse, build, tear down, create, and destroy.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Playing the God-Machine</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God-Machine proper is the sum total of all Command and Control Infrastructure, all facilities, every occult matrix, and every angel. <b>It\u2019s the emergent self-awareness of the magical symbolism of human systems</b>, and it \u201clives\u201d within its entire work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setting aside the matter of birth-order,* it's pretty evident that the Principle deals more with ignition while the Machine is more concerned with completion; they're different sorts of <i>telos</i> for different types of story \u2014 Fire and the Wheel, as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/15681-what-is-your-god-machine?p=15824#post15824\">Arc's highlighted</a>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* Those of you familiar with (at least 2e) Exalted may recall how Oramus is the oldest Primordial despite Cytherea being the first.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T15:31:13-07:00","id":487713,"title":"","content":"The idea of the Principle's true purpose being to help Promethians in their pilgrimage always struck me as ridiculously small in scale and scope for a cosmic entity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T16:03:23-07:00","id":487761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=487713#post487713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of the Principle's true purpose being to help Promethians in their pilgrimage always struck me as ridiculously small in scale and scope for a cosmic entity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless prometheans are a much larger deal on a cosmic scale?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T16:20:31-07:00","id":487768,"title":"","content":"Promethean is generally remarked upon as a pro-humanity game. Maybe the birth of a new human from whole cloth (more or less) is a big, big deal, cosmically speaking? Hence the Principle's great interest in transforming these proto-humans into the real thing.<br /> <br /> Gives me warm fuzzy feelings, that does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T20:16:13-07:00","id":487909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AncientSwordRage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=487761#post487761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless prometheans are a much larger deal on a cosmic scale?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun etymology fact of the day: &quot;Chrysalis&quot; is both the name for the transitional form of a butterfly and derived from the ancient Greek word for &quot;golden.&quot;<br /> <br /> All the world's a powder keg when it comes to the Created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T00:01:38-07:00","id":488038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AncientSwordRage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=487761#post487761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless prometheans are a much larger deal on a cosmic scale?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=487768#post487768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean is generally remarked upon as a pro-humanity game. Maybe the birth of a new human from whole cloth (more or less) is a big, big deal, cosmically speaking? Hence the Principle's great interest in transforming these proto-humans into the real thing.<br /> <br /> Gives me warm fuzzy feelings, that does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I would expect to see rules and charachter creation options that reflect that. At the very least it would have to explain why helping a Promethian is a bigger deal than helping Average Jane in her &quot;pilgramage&quot; to find a husband and have 2.4 kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T03:04:42-07:00","id":488096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=488038#post488038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then I would expect to see rules and charachter creation options that reflect that. At the very least it would have to explain why helping a Promethian is a bigger deal than helping Average Jane in her &quot;pilgramage&quot; to find a husband and have 2.4 kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? I mean, the comment is largely a joke, but if we do start with the assumption that creating a new human soul through alchemy is, in the context of the universe, a Big Deal, then why would you expect mechanics that reflect that? It's a premise, not a thesis that needs to be proven.<br /> <br /> Obviously, helping regular humans isn't as high on the agenda. They already have a proper soul. They already are human. It's the Created that need the help to get to that treasured state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T10:06:12-07:00","id":488418,"title":"","content":"It is not the destination but the journey that is important. For instance if one were to go through heaven and hell just to be human wouldn't that journey have alot of symbolic power? Imagine all the energy and effort put into the pilgrimage from all parties. If the created become just human what did their pilgrimage reap? Or what if them becoming human is the pay off.<br /> <br /> Let's make two assumptions. One, reincarnation occurs in some form or another. Two, though there is a reserve the number of human souls can be reduced by various factors. So the created are the principle trying to restock periodically before stock run low","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T14:17:33-07:00","id":488707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=488096#post488096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? I mean, the comment is largely a joke, but if we do start with the assumption that creating a new human soul through alchemy is, in the context of the universe, a Big Deal, then why would you expect mechanics that reflect that? It's a premise, not a thesis that needs to be proven.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to answer that?<br /> <br /> Reflecting your premise is the core purpose of mechanics. Take Disquiet, it reflects the premise that Prometheans are alone in the world. If the fluff said Promethians were alone and rejected by everyone but there was no mechanical reason I wouldn't buy it.<br /> <br /> Same here. If the fluff says the Pilgramage is so important that supporting it is the purpose of God's existence but nothing in the rules actually suggests the Pilgamage is important I won't buy it either. Rules (probably Merits) for a Forest Gump like charachter who inadvertently inspires major historical events would be a good starting point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-22-2015, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T16:01:18-07:00","id":488811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=488707#post488707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to answer that?<br /> <br /> Reflecting your premise is the core purpose of mechanics. Take Disquiet, it reflects the premise that Prometheans are alone in the world. If the fluff said Promethians were alone and rejected by everyone but there was no mechanical reason I wouldn't buy it.<br /> <br /> Same here. If the fluff says the Pilgramage is so important that supporting it is the purpose of God's existence but nothing in the rules actually suggests the Pilgamage is important I won't buy it either. Rules (probably Merits) for a Forest Gump like charachter who inadvertently inspires major historical events would be a good starting point.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the contrary, I would think that a merit like that would directly take away from such a theme. That's suggesting that in order for a human soul to be important, it has to be important in terms of the human world, do important things, be involved in important events. And yet there's no reason for something &quot;important&quot; from a mortal perspective to be in any way something that impacts on how the Principle perceives the importance of a Promethean's quest to achieve humanity.<br /> <br /> Besides, the Pilgrimage is the centre of the game. The premise of Promethean is that every Promethean is undertaking it. From the perspective of the protagonists, there is nothing given more weight in the context of the game than achieving humanity. Why wouldn't the God-figure who only appears with any primacy in the Promethean game-line share this view?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T10:46:57-07:00","id":489645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=488811#post488811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And yet there's no reason for something &quot;important&quot; from a mortal perspective to be in any way something that impacts on how the Principle perceives the importance of a Promethean's quest to achieve humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div> That is completely and utterly wrong.<br /> <br /> Promethian is a game about discovering what it means to be human. You don't just need to survive for X years and slay Y Pandorans. You actually have to learn about humanity. This means that the setting should reinforce that. As one of the setting's core mysteries and something that Promethians are actively encourage to study via the Mercurius Refinement (Meeting a Quashamal and learning a Quashamal's mission are both sample Milestones) understanding the Principle, or just small fragments of the Principle, should help a Promethian understand humanity.<br /> <br /> Saying that the Principle's core purpose is unrelated to a human point of view goes against this core theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=488811#post488811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why wouldn't the God-figure who only appears with any primacy in the Promethean game-line share this view?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can make understanding why the Principle focuses on the Promethian Pilgramage above all else an enormous insight into understanding humanity then it could work.<br /> <br /> But it would still result in a small and limited setting. One of the things that Promethian did very well was it captured the interplay between the individual and bigger things. Humans are individuals but tying onself to bigger things is a fundamental part of humanity: Religions, nations, philosophies, communities.<br /> <br /> In order to understand humanity Promethians need opportunities to do the same, and explore what happens. Disquiet makes that hard, but assisting a Quashamal, that was a good way to do it. Making the Principle about Promethians defeats the point, you try to participate in something bigger than yourself but it turns out it was about you all along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 04-23-2015, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T13:37:38-07:00","id":489783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=489645#post489645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That is completely and utterly wrong.<br /> <br /> Promethian is a game about discovering what it means to be human. You don't just need to survive for X years and slay Y Pandorans. You actually have to learn about humanity. This means that the setting should reinforce that. As one of the setting's core mysteries and something that Promethians are actively encourage to study via the Mercurius Refinement (Meeting a Quashamal and learning a Quashamal's mission are both sample Milestones) understanding the Principle, or just small fragments of the Principle, should help a Promethian understand humanity.<br /> <br /> Saying that the Principle's core purpose is unrelated to a human point of view goes against this core theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I think we have our wires crossed when it comes to what I was referring to as &quot;important&quot;. Your comment about a Forrest Gump-esque merit putting the Promethean at the centre of human events seemed to be pushing towards an understanding of humanity only from the perspective of exceptional individuals. But that's not even close to the same as understanding the human experience. I was just saying that participation in something that is &quot;important&quot; from a human point of view, namely large political, historical, or economic events that shape the lives of many humans at once, isn't actually tied to the nature of humanity very closely. It might be for a specific Pilgrimage, but there's no reason the Principle needs to find a Promethean discovering the value of relationships through an affair with a waitress at a diner any less important than one discovering about the nature of nationalism and brinksmanship by inadvertently participating in the human missile crisis. Just because one of those events is considered important to humanity at large doesn't mean an entity as alien as the Principle needs to consider an event on that scale as important enough to involve it.<br /> <br /> I absolutely agree about everything you say about learning about humanity. I just disagree with the notion that the Principle can only find the Pilgrimage important if it involves &quot;big&quot; events.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=489645#post489645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can make understanding why the Principle focuses on the Promethian Pilgramage above all else an enormous insight into understanding humanity then it could work.<br /> <br /> But it would still result in a small and limited setting. One of the things that Promethian did very well was it captured the interplay between the individual and bigger things. Humans are individuals but tying onself to bigger things is a fundamental part of humanity: Religions, nations, philosophies, communities.<br /> <br /> In order to understand humanity Promethians need opportunities to do the same, and explore what happens. Disquiet makes that hard, but assisting a Quashamal, that was a good way to do it. Making the Principle about Promethians defeats the point, you try to participate in something bigger than yourself but it turns out it was about you all along.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. Like I said, the original comment was a joke. Defining the goals of an unknowable cosmic tier entity is <i>always</i> going to make the setting smaller. I was just responding to your comment about a lack of mechanics to support such a theme to say that there's a pretty good mechanical backing already, if you want to make that change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T14:28:23-07:00","id":489868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=489783#post489783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I think we have our wires crossed when it comes to what I was referring to as &quot;important&quot;. Your comment about a Forrest Gump-esque merit putting the Promethean at the centre of human events seemed to be pushing towards an understanding of humanity only from the perspective of exceptional individuals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, you definately misread that. I wasn't talking about the Promethian's experiences at all. I was talking about why the Principle focuses on Created.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=489783#post489783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely agree about everything you say about learning about humanity. I just disagree with the notion that the Principle can only find the Pilgrimage important if it involves &quot;big&quot; events.</div> </div> </div> </div> Remember it's not just &quot;important&quot;. It's &quot;most important&quot;.<br /> <br /> Can the Principle care about every last Promethian. Sure. Heck, it might be God and the Church is very clear that God loves every single person.<br /> <br /> But why does the Principle think that this random Golem is more important than that mortal president? Or that Mage? Or that mortal alchemist?<br /> <br /> That's what I'm saying needs mechanical support<ul><li>If studying the Principle can teach a Promethian about humanity</li> <li>Then learning the Principle's reasons for focusing on the Pilgramage will be a Milestone in learning humanity.</li> <li>Which means that those reasons will make sense from a human perspective.</li> <li>If they make sense from a human perspective they'll have a visible effect on the world.</li> <li>That visible effect should have mechanics to let players interact with it.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> The Promethian Forest Gump doesn't interact with big events because he can only learn from big events; he interacts with big events to justify why his Pilgramage is important enough to grab the Principle's attention.<br /> <br /> Basically from a human perspective if the Principle had a choice between helping a random Promethian become human or making sure Hitler got into art school instead of politics; then obviously it makes sense to focus on Hitler. Any Promethian who learned that the Principle choose to focus on the Promethian instead would be moved away from humanity (an anti-milestone?) because at best they wasted their time trying to work out the Principle's inhuman logic, at worst they concluded that if the Principle chose it they should start thinking that way too.<br /> <br /> So the only way you can have the Principle focus on Promethians is if the Created were the Principle's best tools for doing good that humans can recognise. The Principle introduces a Promethian to Hitler. The Created learns about humanity from interacting with him (if only, what not to do) and in the process either save Hitler from becoming evil, kills him, or infects him with some very slow Transmutation that's the real reason why WoD history looks like the real world rather than Nazi's winning the war.<br /> <br /> But if the Principle will keep introducing a Promethian to would-be evil dictators so it can kill them. That should have mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=489783#post489783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course. Like I said, the original comment was a joke. Defining the goals of an unknowable cosmic tier entity is <i>always</i> going to make the setting smaller.</div> </div> </div> </div> Absolutely. But some goals are still more limiting than others.<br /> <br /> For example, saying that the Principle's goal is to guide humanity on a species wide pigramage. Sort of like the god of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whig_history\" target=\"_blank\">Wigg history</a>. That leads to a wider setting than Matt's one simply because it's not about Promethians. It introduces something else to the setting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T18:39:08-07:00","id":490117,"title":"","content":"My own take on it is that the Principle is intrinsically linked to Pyros; and to the extent that it's interested in humanity, it's because Pyros is somehow linked to humanity. The corollary of this is that if Pyros isn't involved in a particular circumstance, then the Principle isn't interested in it, no matter how much involvement of humanity there is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T22:46:48-07:00","id":491395,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Some of us have been around a long time, still walking that road toward the New Dawn, no matter how many decades or eons that takes. Those wizened ramblers like to talk about the universe, from the dandelion seed to the exploding supernova, trying to put them together like a puzzle with no edges. One time, I heard a story. Don't know if it's true. It's about the Principle, the source of all thought and design, and its creation. The spark of the the first fires and the cornerstone of the great monuments wanted to make something that was conscious, that was aware. In essence, it wanted to create a Promethean. It didn't build something like you or I would though, out of flesh and steel. No, it built a thing out of ideas. Concepts linked together until they formed self sustaining strings. Memetically describing both itself and the world it inhabited, until it by the time it was finished the world could never have existed without it being a part. We create life in our image. You or I might construct a man, but the Principle manufactured a god. Does it have a purpose? It believe it does, so it describes itself having one and then describes a world to accommodate that goal. The process is both ongoing and already long finished, each incantation and line of code making things as they always were. Only we can really see it. We weren't born into this world, so when the world changes we don't change with it. They won't believe us if we tell them, that's part of being on the outside. If any of us gets in though... At least according to some hobo bodhisattvas, all bets are off...&quot;<br /> <br /> -Herschel, Tammuz Ophidian</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T08:31:44-07:00","id":491671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/482979-prometheans-and-the-god-machine?p=491395#post491395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;Some of us have been around a long time, still walking that road toward the New Dawn, no matter how many decades or eons that takes. Those wizened ramblers like to talk about the universe, from the dandelion seed to the exploding supernova, trying to put them together like a puzzle with no edges. One time, I heard a story. Don't know if it's true. It's about the Principle, the source of all thought and design, and its creation. The spark of the the first fires and the cornerstone of the great monuments wanted to make something that was conscious, that was aware. In essence, it wanted to create a Promethean. It didn't build something like you or I would though, out of flesh and steel. No, it built a thing out of ideas. Concepts linked together until they formed self sustaining strings. Memetically describing both itself and the world it inhabited, until it by the time it was finished the world could never have existed without it being a part. We create life in our image. You or I might construct a man, but the Principle manufactured a god. Does it have a purpose? It believe it does, so it describes itself having one and then describes a world to accommodate that goal. The process is both ongoing and already long finished, each incantation and line of code making things as they always were. Only we can really see it. We weren't born into this world, so when the world changes we don't change with it. They won't believe us if we tell them, that's part of being on the outside. If any of us gets in though... At least according to some hobo bodhisattvas, all bets are off...&quot;<br /> <br /> -Herschel, Tammuz Ophidian</i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Are you implying that the God-Machine is some kind of Ur-Promethean? Because that's a cool idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T02:19:31-07:00","id":492447,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Principle is trying to create new souls rather than concentrating on the Prometheans themselves? As noted, they seem to be a continually guiding force, they guided humans before they took notice of Prometheans... Perhaps it is the souls that is important to it's Grand Plan, when it reaches whatever it is itself?<br /> <br /> Heck, the Magnum Opus of the Principle could be leading to the creation of the God-Machine. We know it's from the future and not created by human hands, but perhaps something with a soul made it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}